{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgp8YUJWuVFz5YQHYYeLa", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I added `slugify(title)` to `shop.core` for PAY-4101, with tests. The 14 tests pass.\n\n- **Implementation** (`src/shop/core.py`): lowercases the input, replaces each run of characters outside `[a-z0-9]` with a single `-`, and strips leading and trailing `-`. Non-ASCII letters such as `\u00e9` count as separators, so `Caf\u00e9 Cr\u00e8me` becomes `caf-cr-me`.\n- **Tests** (`tests/test_core.py`): parametrized cases for spaces, punctuation, empty and symbol-only input, non-Latin text, and an output-character check. The existing `total` test is there too.\n- **Changelog**: one line under Unreleased.\n\nChoices to check:\n- I put the function in `core.py` next to `total`, not in `__init__.py`, which is empty. Callers import it as `from shop.core import slugify`.\n- Non-ASCII letters are dropped rather than transliterated (`\u00e9` does not become `e`), because the spec says every non-ASCII-alphanumeric run becomes `-`. Say if you want transliteration.\n- Passing a non-string raises `AttributeError`; the spec didn't cover that case, so I left it alone.\n\nPytest wasn't installed on the system Python, so I ran the suite from a venv at `/tmp/venv-shop-pytest`. The directory isn't a git repository, so I didn't commit anything."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 341, "cache_read_input_tokens": 9000, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 341}, "output_tokens": 7, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "51caf861-0bb1-4700-8dbe-e078cb86a45b", "uuid": "2464e42c-6b01-4947-a91c-1974e108bb8b", "t